# Copy to packetrat.env (do not commit).
# An existing Config\mailhawk.env from before the rename is still read when packetrat.env is absent.

# --- Lazarette discovery (prefer env override; Lazarette was formerly ARC) ---
# Resolution order: LAZARETTE_PATH/ROOT/HOME env -> ARC_PATH/ROOT/HOME env ->
#   LAZARETTE_PATH= / ARC_PATH= in this file -> %LOCALAPPDATA%\Lazarette -> %LOCALAPPDATA%\ARC ->
#   sibling clone (Projects\Lazarette, then Projects\arc) -> %USERPROFILE%\Projects\Lazarette, then \arc
# Sibling layout:
#   Projects\PacketRat
#   Projects\Lazarette    <- contains lib\Arc.ps1 or lib\Lazarette.ps1 (a folder named arc still works;
#                            pm.ps1 is only used for ARC 3/4)
# LAZARETTE_PATH=C:\Users\YOU\Projects\Lazarette
# ARC_PATH still works as a fallback.

# --- Optional managed environment tokens (never commit a populated file) ---
# Prefer Lazarette or Configuration > Credentials > Manual (session only).
# Manual tokens submitted through the GUI are NEVER written into this file.
# Only use token environment settings if authorized by your workstation policy.
# AiEndpoint (your organization's AI endpoint) -> AI_ENDPOINT_TOKEN + Lazarette item ai-endpoint-api
# Grok       (Databricks serving endpoint)     -> DATABRICKS_TOKEN  + Lazarette item grok-api
# AI_ENDPOINT_TOKEN=
# DATABRICKS_TOKEN=
# Deprecated names are still read: the former AI-endpoint token variable, and the former vault item
# names when the items above are absent (see Private/PacketRatLlm.ps1 and Private/LazaretteBridge.ps1).

# --- Lazarette item name overrides (optional; defaults are canonical) ---
# PACKETRAT_LAZARETTE_ITEM_AiEndpoint=ai-endpoint-api
# PACKETRAT_LAZARETTE_ITEM_Grok=grok-api
# Former override names are still read as fallbacks (former PacketRat/MailHawk names, then
# Halyard's shared HALYARD_LAZARETTE_ITEM_* names and its previous names).

# --- AI endpoints ---
# AiEndpoint defaults to the local phoenix-lai server on this PC (loopback only, model phoenixlai):
#   http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1/chat/completions
# A token is optional there (phoenix-lai's API key is off by default). Set this to use another endpoint:
# PACKETRAT_AI_ENDPOINT_URL=https://ai.example.org/v1/chat/completions
# Grok is an outside provider with no built-in URL; set this to use it:
# PACKETRAT_GROK_URL=https://databricks.example.org/serving-endpoints/<endpoint>/invocations
# Shared override for whichever profile is used:
# LLM_URL=
# LLM_MODEL=
# PACKETRAT_LLM_PROFILE=Auto          # Auto | Grok | AiEndpoint (the former profile name still works)

# --- Triage ---
# Your organization's mail domain(s), comma-separated, for the organization-domain triage rules.
# A domain suffix also works. When unset, those rules never match.
# PACKETRAT_ORG_DOMAIN=example.org

# --- Fleet intelligence router (Fairlead), opt-in and off by default ---
# PACKETRAT_ROUTER=fairlead
# PACKETRAT_FAIRLEAD_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8776/v1/chat/completions
# PACKETRAT_FAIRLEAD_MODEL=auto
# PACKETRAT_FAIRLEAD_PRIVACY=local
# FAIRLEAD_TOKEN is Fairlead's own key (only if Fairlead is not on this PC). Never a provider token, and not stored here.

# --- Lifecycle ---
# Closing the PacketRat browser tab stops the local PowerShell service (20 s after the last
# heartbeat, never during a scan). Set to 0 to keep it running (same as Launch-PacketRat.bat --stay).
# The former MAILHAWK_AUTO_STOP name is still read when this one is unset.
# PACKETRAT_AUTO_STOP=1

# --- Outlook ---
# PACKETRAT_MAX_EMAILS=40
# PACKETRAT_BODY_PREVIEW_CHARS=280
# PACKETRAT_PROVIDER=COM
# Every PACKETRAT_* setting falls back to its former MAILHAWK_* name when unset.

# Credential source can be chosen live in the browser GUI:
#  - Lazarette / configured environment: existing Lazarette bridge and env fallback.
#  - Manual: token held in process memory until server stops or user clears it.
# Do not paste a manual token in this template.

# Privacy: raw AI output may include sensitive mail content; not saved by default.
# Only if approved for debugging: PACKETRAT_SAVE_RAW_AI=1
